28011	28121	28134	28134	Panteley	65	" Two merchants , father and son , were travelling , selling holy images . They put up in the inn not far from here that is now kept by Ignat Fomin . The old man had a drop too much , and began boasting that he had a lot of money with him . We all know merchants are a boastful set , God preserve us . . . . They ca n't resist showing off before the likes of us . And at the time some mowers were staying the night at the inn . So they overheard what the merchants said and took note of it . "
